{"type":"text","timestamp":1786608958990,"sessionID":"ses_005cf0068ffe0wWmqZmErIJ3Az","part":{"id":"prt_ffa3138db001Ppqy5X4Xa62AAj","messageID":"msg_ffa312d50001PMsLxl973ZSSiV","sessionID":"ses_005cf0068ffe0wWmqZmErIJ3Az","type":"text","text":"The seed is an unrelated Flask application, so I’ll replace it rather than layering protocols onto it. The implementation will use one `websockets` listener: WebSocket upgrades handle notifications, while HTTP `POST /health` accepts a SOAP envelope and returns the connected count; ordinary REST `GET /health` will not be exposed.","time":{"start":1786608957659,"end":1786608958984},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_03334f34916aec8e016a7d7d3d9a708191aac69b06c363687f","phase":"commentary"}}}}
